WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.187
Welcome to Grade 5 English, Unit 9: Lights, Camera, Action…

2
00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:10.842
Unit 9 is about scripts: the writing that actors
follow on a stage and in front of a camera.

3
00:00:10.922 --> 00:00:17.062
You will read “The Forest Guardians” first
as a play script and then as a film script,

4
00:00:17.142 --> 00:00:22.921
comparing stage directions with camera
directions such as pan, zoom and close-up.

5
00:00:23.001 --> 00:00:28.418
You will also study compound nouns like
woodland, footpath and bamboo grove,

6
00:00:28.498 --> 00:00:31.889
and write and perform a short scene of your own.

7
00:00:31.969 --> 00:00:35.361
The unit story, “Nookwatch: The Forest Mission”,

8
00:00:35.441 --> 00:00:41.654
follows Amal and Sami as they help rescue
an injured lemur at a woodland rescue centre.

9
00:00:41.734 --> 00:00:47.729
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:47.809 --> 00:00:54.403
By the end of this unit, you will be able to
recognise the layout and features of a play script,

11
00:00:54.483 --> 00:00:59.964
including the cast list, character names,
colons, dialogue and stage directions.

12
00:01:00.044 --> 00:01:05.317
You will also explain the difference
between a play script and a film script,

13
00:01:05.397 --> 00:01:09.488
using examples from both versions of “The Forest Guardians”.

14
00:01:09.568 --> 00:01:14.841
You will also read stage directions
accurately and locate upstage, downstage,

15
00:01:14.921 --> 00:01:18.665
centre stage and the entrances and exits they describe.

16
00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:21.237
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

17
00:01:21.317 --> 00:01:27.285
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
nook, woodland, bamboo, groove, fertile, textbook.

18
00:01:27.365 --> 00:01:32.387
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

19
00:01:32.467 --> 00:01:36.356
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

20
00:01:36.436 --> 00:01:42.119
The reading sequence includes The Forest
Guardians: a play script and The Forest Guardians:

21
00:01:42.199 --> 00:01:44.146
the same scene as a film script.

22
00:01:44.226 --> 00:01:45.032
Read actively.

23
00:01:45.112 --> 00:01:49.402
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

24
00:01:49.482 --> 00:01:53.518
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

25
00:01:53.598 --> 00:01:57.238
The first language focus is What a Compound Noun Is.

26
00:01:57.318 --> 00:02:03.248
A compound noun joins two or more words so
that together they name one single thing.

27
00:02:03.328 --> 00:02:09.830
Knowing the parts lets you work out a new word
without reaching for a dictionary every time.

28
00:02:09.910 --> 00:02:17.627
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

29
00:02:17.707 --> 00:02:21.904
In speaking, you will complete
Speaking 1: Read the Script Aloud.

30
00:02:21.984 --> 00:02:26.312
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

31
00:02:26.392 --> 00:02:29.668
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

32
00:02:29.748 --> 00:02:33.155
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

33
00:02:33.235 --> 00:02:34.761
You are ready to begin.

34
00:02:34.841 --> 00:02:41.671
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

35
00:02:41.751 --> 00:02:45.021
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

36
00:02:45.101 --> 00:02:52.769
Use AI English for hints and feedback any time, and bring
your questions to a live session too if you join one.
